{"id": "EUVD-2026-104689", "enisaUuid": "e9aaf1e0-b849-3300-8bb0-ecb2df35e157", "description": "DB-GPT through 0.8.2 contains a hardcoded credentials vulnerability in its default docker-compose.yml that sets a static MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and publishes port 3306 on all interfaces. Attackers reaching port 3306 or the shared dbgptnet network can authenticate as root@% to gain full database access including FILE and SUPER privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T13:49:14", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-77933", "https://github.com/eosphoros-ai/DB-GPT/blob/83609c471266607490b24e72188311efa23a0d16/docker-compose.yml#L9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/db-gpt-through-0.8.2-hardcoded-mysql-root-credentials-in-docker-compose-deployment"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-77933", "GHSA-rq79-8cw2-45h7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "54d86df2-9196-3d17-b683-b1008e144fa6", "product": {"name": "db-gpt", "vendor": {"name": "eosphoros-ai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.8.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91fdf699-a7f9-35fc-a5fd-9de816a3b9c6", "vendor": {"name": "eosphoros-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}